{"diagnosis": "Fetch TB with 256 NOPs (0x00000013 with bits[1:0]=2'b11) traps with TRAP asserted and FAIL 0xdead at 2009 cycles instead of sequential progress. Expected compressed_instr==0 for 32-bit ops but excerpt holds it at 1. Root cause at line 892: `compressed_instr <= 1` as default makes every 32-bit instruction decode as 16-bit compressed, corrupting PC step/alignment and causing trap.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -892,3 +892,3 @@
-			compressed_instr <= 1;
+			compressed_instr <= 0;
 			if (COMPRESSED_ISA && mem_rdata_latched[1:0] != 2'b11) begin
 				compressed_instr <= 1;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (no 0xdead), TRAP not asserted, fetch alignment/progress OK through NOP sled"}

